$DIR/test.p:28:12: Slot2 must be declared owner: Slot2 is defined from Slot, which is an owner
    An owner owns memory or another resource and releases it when it is dropped,
    so it moves instead of being copied. A type defined from an owner owns the
    same things.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    Plutonium does not make Slot2 an owner silently; the keyword is written in
    its declaration, so that a change to the type of a field elsewhere is
    reported here, at the declaration, and not at every place that copies a
    value. Write owner after the name:
        type Slot2 owner Slot
    (see "Owner types" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.18)
    (run "pluto explain E3202" for a longer explanation)

